132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (Living Without Barriers is a renovation project focused on redesigning an existing Muskoka cottage for a client living with Multiple Sclerosis. The design prioritizes accessibility, independence, and safety through open circulation, accessible storage, and barrier-free kitchen and bathroom design. The project was developed through interdisciplinary collaboration with Occupational Therapy students, which informed accessibility requirements such as turning radius, reach ranges, and safe circulation paths. The final design demonstrates how interior design can support independence, comfort, and quality of life through accessible and human-centered design strategies while maintaining a warm cottage environment connected to the surrounding landscape.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
